        "comments": "The assembly bFalPer5.hap1.1 is based on 72x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Chromosomes Z was identified through synteny analysis with Falco cherrug (GCF_023634085.1) and copy number in the diploid assembly.Chromosomes W was identified by copy number in the diploid assembly.The karyotype of Falco peregrinus (2n = 50) is described by Nanda et al. (2007) [https://doi.org/10.1007/s10577-007-1210-6]. In this assembly, one microchromosome could not be identified, resulting in one fewer autosome than expected.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 1 (104,637 - 105,656 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 5 (87,779 - 89,386 Kbp) are unknown.The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 10 (22,856 - 28,736 Kbp) are unknown.",
